      "contentType": "text/html; charset=utf-8",
      "pageTitle": "Digispace Africa Research Fellowship 2027 | Application Form",
      "pageDescription": "SHAPE AFRICA&#39;S DIGITAL FUTURE\nAre you curious about how technology is shaping Africa&#39;s future? Do you have ideas about digital rights, emerging technologies or the policies affecting our connected societies?\nThe Digispace Africa Research Fellowship brings together emerging African researchers, professionals and changemakers to explore digital challenges and contribute fresh perspectives to digital policy and governance.\nThrough expert-led sessions, mentorship, peer learning and guided research, fellows develop practical research skills and contribute to Africa&#39;s digital future.\nWhat you can look forward to:\n• Learn from digital policy experts and researchers.\n• Develop a policy-oriented research paper.\n• Connect with professionals across Africa.\n• Present your research and join",
      "evidenceText": "Digispace Africa Research Fellowship 2027 | Application Form Digispace Africa Research Fellowship 2027 | Application Form SHAPE AFRICA'S DIGITAL FUTURE Are you curious about how technology is shaping Africa's future? Do you have ideas about digital rights, emerging technologies or the policies affecting our connected societies? The Digispace Africa Research Fellowship brings together emerging African researchers, professionals and changemakers to explore digital challenges and contribute fresh perspectives to digital policy and governance. Through expert-led sessions, mentorship, peer learning and guided research, fellows develop practical research skills and contribute to Africa's digital future. What you can look forward to: • Learn from digital policy experts and researchers. • Develop a policy-oriented research paper. • Connect with professionals across Africa. • Present your research and join our alumni community. Programme Timeline The Digispace Africa Research Fellowship 2027 is scheduled to run from 11 January to 18 June 2027 , combining virtual learning, mentorship, independent research and a concluding Research Symposium. Key Dates Applications open: 9 November 2026 Application deadline: 7 December 2026, 11:59 PM GMT Selection notifications: 21–22 December 2026 Fellowship orientation: 11 January 2027 Expert-led learning sessions: January – March 2027 Research development and mentorship: January – April 2027 First research draft: 25 March 2027 Final research submission: 30 April 2027 Research Symposium and Graduation: 18 June 2027 Participation Expectations The Fellowship is fully virtual and combines expert-led sessions, research development, mentorship and peer engagement. Selected fellows will be expected to: Attend scheduled virtual learning sessions and participate actively in discussions. Dedicate time to independent research and preparation between sessions. Engage constructively with mentors and research reviewers. Complete research assignments and meet agreed submission deadlines. Participate in the concluding Research Symposium and Graduation, as applicable. Please note: The Fellowship requires a consistent commitment throughout the programme. Applicants are encouraged to consider their academic, professional and personal schedules before applying. A detailed programme calendar, including session times and research milestones, will be shared with selected fellows during onboarding. Application Enquiries and Submission Policy For enquiries or technical difficulties relating to the application process, please contact us at info@digispaceafrica.org . Please note that all applications must be submitted through the official online application form. Applications submitted via email will not be accepted. Sign in to Google to save your progress. Learn more * Indicates required question Email * Your email Next Page 1 of 4 Clear form Never submit passwords through Google Forms. This content is neither created nor endorsed by Google. - Terms of Service - Privacy Policy Does this form look suspicious? Report   Forms       Help and feedback       Contact form owner       Help Forms improve       Report",
