      "evidenceText": "AI Launchpad Startup Grants | Zoom AI Services Zoom for startups AI Launchpad Startup Grants Empowering the next generation of AI-native founders with the tools, credits, and community to build what's next. Applications are open. Limited spots available. Apply Now Build the Future of AI — We'll Help You Get There AI Launchpad is a grant program designed for startups building innovative products powered by artificial intelligence. We provide the resources you need to move fast, ship early, and scale confidently — including access to our full suite of AI Services and cutting-edge speech and language APIs, from real-time transcription and translation to natural language understanding, decision intelligence and voice generation. Major perks What You Get Up to $150,000 in Credits Access generous platform credits to build with Zoom's powerful STT, Translation, Summarization, Decisions and Voice Agent capabilities. With the accuracy, speed, and reliability your product demands, all on a single voice AI platform. Priority API Access Eligible startups may receive early access to new models, features, and APIs, depending on their program tier and availability. Technical Support Access technical guidance and support to integrate, optimize, and scale your product, with support levels varying by program tier. Founder Network Join an exclusive community of AI founders, investors, and mentors. Share learnings, get introductions, and grow together. Co-Marketing Opportunities Opportunity to be featured in our blog, social channels, and partner newsletters. We'll help amplify your story to thousands of developers and investors. Exclusive Workshops Access private sessions on AI product development, fundraising, go-to-market strategy, and more — led by industry experts. Who Should Apply We’re looking for ambitious startups and emerging companies building AI-first products. You’re a great fit if you: Are an early- to growth-stage startup Have a small to mid-sized product and engineering team Are building a product or service with AI at its core Have a working prototype, production product, or clear technical roadmap Have a use case that can benefit from AI APIs, real-time AI, voice, speech, translation, agents, or enterprise AI infrastructure Are ready to move fast, integrate new AI capabilities, and iterate with customers Ready to Launch? Applications are now open. Apply today to start building with Zoom AI Services. Apply Now How It Works Apply Online Fill out our short application form. It takes less than 10 minutes. Tell us about your team, your product, and how you plan to use AI. Review & Interview Our team reviews every application. Shortlisted founders will be invited to a brief 20-minute call with our team. Get Accepted Accepted startups receive their grant package, including credits, onboarding materials, and community access. Build & Grow Start building. We'll check in regularly to offer support, surface opportunities, and celebrate your milestones. Program Tiers Compare credits and benefits across the Seed, Growth, and Scale tiers. Feature 🌱 Seed Tier 🚀 Growth Tier ⚡ Scale Tier Platform Credits $5,000 $50,000 $150,000 New API Access Standard Priority Early Access Technical Support Community Shared CSM Dedicated Engineer Co-Marketing — Not included ✓ Included ✓ Featured Investor Introductions — Not included — Not included ✓ Included Frequently Asked Questions Can I apply if I'm outside the United States? Yes. We welcome applications from eligible startups worldwide, subject to applicable laws, regulations, and program eligibility requirements. See Terms and Conditions . What stage does my startup need to be at? We support startups from pre-seed through growth stage, from teams building their first product to companies scaling AI products in production. Funding stage is not a strict requirement — we evaluate each application based on the product, team, technical fit, and potential to build and scale with Zoom AI Services. How long does the grant last? Credits are valid for 12 months from the date of issuance. Community access and support benefits are available for the 12-month program period. Can I apply if I've already received funding? Yes. Having prior funding does not disqualify you. We look at the quality of your product, team, and vision — not just your funding status. How many startups are accepted per cohort? We accept a limited number of startups based on program capacity and eligibility. Applications are reviewed on a rolling basis. Connect with us Apply now Complete all required fields marked with an asterisk (*). Applications are reviewed on a rolling basis. No Zoom account? Sign up before applying. Step 1 of 5 Section 1: Applicant Information Applicant First Name * Applicant Last Name * Applicant Job Title * Applicant LinkedIn URL * Applicant Business Email Address * Zoom Account Email Address * Section 2: Company Information Company Name * Company Legal Name * Company Registration Number * Company Website * Phone Number * Company Address * Street, City, State, Country Section 3: Location Select the region that best represents your company's primary place of business: Location Region * Africa Europe India & South Asia Japan & Korea North America Oceania South America East Asia & Pacific Middle East Section 4: Product & Use Case What does your company/app do? * What are you aiming to build with Zoom? * Stage of Development * Idea / Pre-Seed Prototype / MVP Early Stage (Seed) Growth Stage (Series A/B) Expansion Stage (Series C+) Mature / Enterprise Estimated Number of Users Are people using your product yet? * Yes No What other platforms or solutions have you evaluated or used? Which Zoom AI Services APIs are you interested in using? (Select all that apply) Learn more about products available under Zoom AI Services at Zoom.ai . Scribe API (Speech-to-Text) Text-to-Speech API Speech Summarization API Text Summarization API Interpreter API (Speech Translation) Translator API (Text Translation) Voice Agent API Decisions API Other / Future AI APIs (please specify) Please specify other APIs you would like to see available on Zoom AI Services Section 5: Partner Program Are you applying through a Partner / Accelerator Program? * Yes No Partner / Accelerator Name Partner Contact Email By submitting this form, you confirm that all information provided is accurate and that your startup meets the eligibility requirements for the Zoom AI Launchpad Grants Program. Responses are subject to Zoom's Privacy Statement which you acknowledge that you've read and understand. By submitting this application, you also agree to the Zoom AI Launchpad Program Terms & Conditions , including eligibility requirements, grant usage restrictions, and program obligations. Participation in the Zoom AI Launchpad Startup Grants Program is subject to Zoom's review and approval at its sole discretion. Back Continue Submitting your application... 🎉 Application Received! Thank you for applying to the Zoom AI Launchpad Startup Grants Program . We're excited to learn more about what you're building. Applications are evaluated on a rolling basis — if additional information is needed, a member of our team will reach out. Back TERMS AND CONDITIONS Close Zoom AI Startup Grants Program 1. Overview The Zoom AI Startup Grants Program provides, at Zoom's sole discretion, selected eligible startups and small companies with access to a Zoom Grant Plan (as defined below), including a defined allocation of complimentary AI service credits, for a period of twelve (12) months (the \"Program\"). These Zoom AI Startup Grants Program Terms and Conditions (\"Grant Terms\") govern your participation in the Program and supplement the Zoom Terms of Service (\"Terms of Service\") and Zoom Build Platform Terms of Service (\"Build Platform Terms\") (collectively with the Terms of Service, the \"Underlying Terms\"), which are hereby incorporated by reference. By participating in the Program, selected companies (each such entity, a \"Participant\") agree to be bound by these Grant Terms and the Underlying Terms (collectively, the \"Agreement\"). These Grant Terms apply in addition to the Underlying Terms, except where expressly stated otherwise. In the event of any conflict between these Grant Terms and the Underlying Terms, these Grant Terms shall govern solely with respect to Participant's participation in the Program. Capitalized terms used but not defined in these Grants Terms shall have the meanings set forth in the Underlying Terms. 2. Eligibility The Program is open to eligible startups and emerging companies building AI-driven products or services, as determined by Zoom in its sole discretion. Participants must not be located in, organized under the laws of, or ordinarily resident in any country or territory subject to United States export controls or sanctions, including but not limited to Belarus, Cuba, Iran, North Korea, the sanctioned Ukrainian regions (Crimea, Donetsk, Kherson, Luhansk and Zaporizhzhia), and Russia. The Program is void where prohibited by law. Applicants must provide complete and accurate information regarding their intended use of Zoom's AI Services. The Program is limited to one grant per Participant. 3. Grant Benefits Each approved Participant will receive a Grant subscription plan (\"Grant Plan\") that will include an allocation of complimentary AI Services credits (\"Complimentary Credits\" or \"Credits\") as part of Participant's Build Platform Developer account (\"Account\"). The Credits allocated to Participant's Account are based on Participant's assigned Program tier, as determined by Zoom in its sole discretion. Credit allocations by tier are as follows: Tier 1 – Launch: Up to five thousand dollars ($5,000) in Complimentary Credits. Includes access to full suite of Zoom AI Services APIs. Eligible for community Zoom Team Chat access and monthly group office hours. Tier 2 – Scale: Up to fifty thousand dollars ($50,000) in Complimentary Credits. Eligible for a shared engineering Zoom Chat channel, office hours, and GTM co-marketing support including a dedicated blog post and demo video. Tier 3 – Propel: Up to one hundred and fifty thousand dollars ($150,000) in Complimentary Credits. Eligible for a named senior engineering contact, 1:1 office hours, joint press release opportunities, and co-sell introductions to Zoom's enterprise sales team. Tier assignment is determined by Zoom in its sole discretion based on factors such as the applicant’s business stage, product maturity, technical fit, and anticipated use of Zoom AI Services. Participants will be notified of their assigned tier in the offer letter. Credits are provisioned to the Participant's Zoom Developer Account Project ID within forty-eight (48) hours of signed acceptance. 4. Credit Consumption Credits are not transferrable or assignable to any other account and unused Credits will expire at the end of the twelve (12) month Program period and may not be carried over or redeemed for cash or any other value. One Credit is equivalent to One US Dollar and usage of the AI Services will be converted into Credits where the consumption of Credits will be based on the consumption rates located in this table . In the event Participant uses its entire allotment of Credits before the end of the twelve (12) month Program period, Participant will be charged overage based on the consumption rates in the above table and as set forth in Participant's Order Form. Participant is responsible for usage charges exceeding available Credits. Such charges will be billed monthly in arrears through Participant’s registered billing account. Participant must maintain a valid payment method or other approved billing arrangement. 5. Program Expiration; Options Upon the earlier occurrence of either (a) the conclusion of the twelve (12) month Program period, or (b) Participant's exhaustion of all Credits allocated under their assigned tier, Participant will have the option to convert to a paid Zoom Build Platform subscription plan. Any unused Credits will expire at the end of the twelve (12) month Program period. Participants may apply for a tier upgrade during the twelve (12) month Program period subject to re-evaluation and approval by Zoom in its sole discretion. 6. Branding and Promotion Zoom reserves the right to use Participant's name and branding for promotional purposes in connection with the Program. Participant hereby grants Zoom, its Affiliates, and their respective agents an irrevocable, perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive, sublicensable, transferable, fully paid-up, royalty-free license to use, reproduce, publish, and display Participant's name, logo, and other trademarks or service marks solely in connection with the foregoing. 7. Restrictions Participant can only apply Complimentary Credits to Participant's use of the AI Services included as part of the Build Platform Service. Participant cannot apply the complimentary Credits to usage of any additional products and services available with the Zoom Build Platform under the Account. Participant represents, covenants, and warrants that it will use the AI Services and Complimentary Credits only in compliance with the Agreement. Zoom may independently conduct limited periodic reviews of Participant's use of the AI Services and Complimentary Credits to ensure compliance with the Agreement. 8. Application and Notification Applications are accepted on a rolling basis while the Program is operational. Zoom will use commercially reasonable efforts to provide a decision within one (1) month of submission, but timing may vary. 9. Termination and Compliance Zoom reserves the right to cancel a Grant Plan and/or terminate Participant participation in the Program at any time in Zoom’s sole discretion. 10. Miscellaneous Zoom reserves the right to modify, suspend, or terminate the Program or these Grant Terms at any time, with or without notice, at Zoom's sole discretion. Zoom will exercise commercially reasonable business efforts to provide notice to Participant of material changes to these Grant Terms. Any such notice may be provided to participants via email or through the Zoom platform. 11. Contact For questions or to discuss scaling options, please contact ai-startups@zoom.us .",
