      "pageDescription": "Free tools and techniques.",
      "evidenceText": "Workshop video: Monitoring keywords and webpages This website uses cookies Read our Privacy policy and Terms of use for more information . Accept Customize Decline Workshop video: Monitoring keywords and webpages Free tools and techniques. Craig Silverman Nov 2, 2026 During our October members-only workshop, I showed free tools and techniques for monitoring keywords and webpages. I also covered how to set up alerts that catch new mentions of people, companies, and phrases, how to track changes to webpages, and more. The workshop was partly based on my two recent guides: 12 free tools for monitoring webpages and keywords and Reddit OSINT: What still works for search, monitoring, and archives . Watch the full recording below, and access the transcript, presentation slides, and AI-generated notes. Our next workshop will be in late November. If you aren't a member yet, upgrade today to join our next live workshop. You'll instantly unlock the session materials and our complete archive of past workshop recordings, transcripts, and notes. Upgrade to read the rest Become a paying member of Indicator to access all of our content and our monthly members-only workshop. Support independent media while building your skills. Upgrade Already a subscriber? Sign in A membership gets you : Everything we publish, plus archival content, including the Academic Library Detailed resources like, \"The Indicator Guide to connecting websites together using OSINT tools and methods\" Live monthly workshops and access to all recordings and transcripts Keep Reading Indicator is your essential guide to understanding and investigating digital deception. Subscribe for free I consent to receive newsletters via email. Sign up Terms of service . ABOUT ARCHIVE UPGRADE",
